.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt SYSEXTCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sysextctl
.Nd manage kernel extension policy and boot activation
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm status | list | config | reload | restore
.Nm
.Cm status | load | allow | deny | reset | enable | disable
.Ar module
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
contacts the
.Dq system.SystemExtension
capability service using the caller's discovery authority.
All changes to policy are validated and persisted by the service.
The client does not edit configuration files or invoke
.Xr kldload 2 .
.Pp
The inspection commands
.Pq Cm status , list , config
use the full service when the caller reaches it, and otherwise its
read-only view,
.Dq system.SystemExtension.Status .
.Xr switchboard 8
resolves the read-only view for a process with effective UID 0, outside any
jail, that holds no software grant: a root login shell, a cron job, or a
command started from
.Pa /etc/rc.local
after
.Pa /etc/rc
exits
.Pq Pa /Capabilities/Config/switchboard/root-query.ucl .
The view has no operation that loads a module or changes policy.
Other users reach neither endpoint and get nothing.
The load and policy commands never use the read-only view.
.Pp
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width disable
.It Cm status
Print what the kernel and the broker report, read-only:
the modules compiled into the kernel, the module files loaded since boot
(from
.Xr kldstat 2
and
.Xr modstat 2 ) ,
and the broker's recent load decisions, oldest first.
Each decision names the module, the requesting switchboard client label,
and the outcome: loaded, already loaded, or the reason it was refused
.Po
not on the allow-list and not a hardware driver of this kernel;
client may load hardware drivers only; denied by an administrator override;
or the load failed with an error
.Pc .
The broker keeps the 64 most recent decisions in memory since it started.
Requests that never reach the broker, such as a direct
.Xr kldload 8
refused by the module-loading gate or a
.Nm Cm load
from a shell without a grant, are not decisions and are not listed.
This command needs the read-only view and fails with
.Dv EX_UNAVAILABLE
for any other caller.
.It Cm list
Print permitted module names and their current state,
.Dq loaded
or
.Dq allowed ,
using bounded, lexical discovery.
An entry marked allowed is permitted but not currently loaded.
Each entry also includes an
.Dq installed
field: yes, no, or unknown.
This checks for a regular file named after the entry, with an optional
.Pa .ko
suffix, in the directories specified by
.Va kern.module_path
as visible to the caller.
An inaccessible search path or failed query yields unknown unless a file is found.
This is a file-presence check; it does not resolve module aliases through
.Pa linker.hints
or verify dependencies, compatibility, or package registration.
Each returned entry is coherent; the entire enumeration is not a snapshot
across concurrent edits.
.It Cm config
Show permission, desired boot activation, current loaded state, installed file
presence, and whether
an administrator override exists for each known policy entry.
This is a policy listing, not a catalogue of installed packages.
Loaded state is not disclosed for denied modules.
.It Cm status Ar module
Show the same information for one module.
Over the read-only view, the broker's recent load decisions for that module
follow.
.It Cm load Ar module
Ensure a permitted module is loaded for this boot.
An already loaded module is success.
Only a caller holding a software grant for the service reaches it:
.Pa /etc/rc
and its descendants while
.Pa /etc/rc
runs, and, after boot,
.Xr devd 8
and its actions
.Pq hardware drivers only; see Xr BSDExtension 8 .
A login shell has no such grant, and the service is unavailable to it
.Pq Dv EX_UNAVAILABLE ;
as root it can inspect with
.Cm status .
.It Cm allow Ar module
Persist an administrator permission to load this module.
Permission does not install, authenticate, or load module code.
.It Cm deny Ar module
Persist a denial of future load requests and restoration.
An existing desired boot activation is retained but reported as blocked.
.It Cm reset Ar module
Remove the entire administrator override, including desired activation,
returning permission to the shipped policy.
.It Cm enable Ar module
Persist desired boot activation of an already permitted module.
Use
.Cm load
for immediate activation, or
.Cm restore
to apply all enabled entries.
.It Cm disable Ar module
Remove desired boot activation while retaining any permission override.
This does not forcibly unload shared kernel code.
.It Cm reload
Reread the service's shipped configuration through its Config descriptor.
Administrator overrides are preserved.
Malformed replacements leave the previous policy intact.
.It Cm restore
Load permitted entries with desired boot activation.
The late
.Pa /etc/rc.d/kld
service invokes this after local filesystems mount, even with an empty
.Va kld_list .
.El
.Pp
.Cm allow , deny , reset , enable , disable , reload ,
and
.Cm restore
require ADMIN rights on the service channel, not merely UID 0.
Persistent overrides live in
.Pa /etc/bsdextension/overrides.ucl ,
in a private directory delivered to the service by descriptor.
They survive package updates.
The service validates and syncs a replacement before publishing it to clients.
Requests already admitted under an earlier policy may finish.
.Pp
The administrator directory is on the root filesystem and is read before
serving requests, including bootstrap loads.
It does not depend on the ZFS-backed filesystem service, which may itself
need an extension to start.
This supports UFS installations and read-only installer media; edits on
read-only media fail without changing the active policy.
Missing or corrupt administrator state fails closed, except that an absent
overrides file in the delivered directory means no overrides.
.Pp
There is no force-unload command.
Disabling activation or denying permission leaves existing kernel code loaded
until reboot or normal ownership reclamation permits removal.
Session and boot loads carry a boot-long ownership claim.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /Capabilities/System/SystemExtension.cap/Units/bsdextension.unit/Config/bsdextension.ucl
Shipped defaults; the allowed_extensions array replaces built-in defaults.
.It Pa /etc/bsdextension/overrides.ucl
Versioned administrator state.
Manage it through this command rather than editing storage internals.
.It Pa /Capabilities/Config/switchboard/root-query.ucl
Read-only endpoints switchboard resolves for UID 0 sessions without a grant.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success.
.Cm status
returns 1 for a denied or unloaded module.
Persistent operations return
.Dv EX_TEMPFAIL
if administrator configuration has not been attached.
Other errors use
.Xr sysexits 3
codes.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Why did a driver not load, from a root login shell:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# sysextctl status if_axge
if_axge: allowed, boot=disabled, loaded=yes, installed=yes, policy=default
  2026-11-01 05:12:09 load if_axge (client devd): loaded
# sysextctl status
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr BSDExtension 8 ,
.Xr kldload 8 ,
.Xr switchboard 8
